      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Lexical retrieval can find an exact identifier, while vector retrieval can find related wording. Their raw scores use different scales. Reciprocal rank fusion instead adds a contribution determined by each passage rank in each list. Keep ranks one-based and remove duplicates inside a branch so repetition cannot manufacture extra support.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 22.479999999999997,
          "duration": 22.08,
          "until": 23.129999999999995
        },
        {
          "say": "These supplied lists initially give the two required passages equal fused scores. An additional authorized rewrite branch changes their order. That can improve a retrieval candidate set, yet the generated rewrite remains query expansion rather than evidence. A reranker and held-out labels still need to test which passages are useful for the actual question.",
          "start": 23.129999999999995,
          "end": 45.114,
          "duration": 21.984,
          "until": 45.763999999999996
        }
